    "title": "Michigan-UConn TV info, what time is NCAA championship game tonight?",
    "text": "April 6, 2026, 7:32 p.m. ETCan Michigan basketball end the Big Ten's national championship drought in the NCAA Tournament?It's something that Dusty May and the No. 1-seeded Wolverines will look to do on Monday night at Lucas Oil Stadium when they meet up with No. 2-seeded UConn in the Men's NCAA Tournament national championship game.The Wolverines and the Huskies are set for an 8:50 p.m. ET tip-off inside Lucas Oil Stadium on Monday.Stream Michigan vs. UConn basketball with Sling TVMichigan steamrolled No. 1 Arizona in the Final Four on Saturday to return to the national title game for the first time since 2018, and did so without Yaxel Lendeborg on the court for most of the game. The status and health of the Big Ten Player of the Year will be a big if on whether the Wolverines can cut down the nets on Monday. Lendeborg, who told reporters late Saturday that he'll play Monday, was officially diagnosed with a bone bruise and is dealing with a low-grade MCL sprain in his left knee and an ankle sprain after getting injured in the first half on a layup attempt.The Huskies have been the standard in college basketball the last four seasons under Dan Hurley, as the Big East powerhouse is looking for its third title in the last four years. A few players that the Wolverines will have to stop from getting hot on Monday include former Wolverine forward Tarris Reed Jr., Alex Karaban and Braylon Mullins, with the matchup of Reed and Aday Mara being a highly anticipated one.Here's everything to know about Monday's national championship game:What TV channel is Michigan vs. UConn basketball on tonight?TV channel: TBS | TNT | truTVStreaming options: March Madness Live app | Sling TVTBS will broadcast Monday's national championship game between Michigan and UConn. There will be simulcasts on TNT and truTV as well. Ian Eagle, Bill Raftery and Grant Hill will call the game with Tracy Wolfson reporting from the sidelines.Streaming options for the game include the March Madness Live app (with a TV login) and Sling TV.Michigan vs. UConn basketball start timeDate: Monday, April 6Time: 8:50 p.m. ETLocation: Lucas Oil Stadium (Indianapolis)Michigan and UConn will tip off at 8:50 p.m. ET on Monday, April 6 inside Lucas Oil Stadium in Indianapolis.Stream Michigan vs. UConn basketball with Sling TVMichigan vs. UConn basketball odds, picks, predictionsOdds courtesy of BetMGM as of Monday, April 6Spread: Michigan -6.5Over/under: 145.5Moneyline: Michigan (-285) | UConn (+230)Our editors independently choose our recommendations. Some content is produced with paid support from a third party, however our editorial decisions remain independent. If you buy through our links, the USA TODAY Network may earn a commission. Prices and availability may change.",
